# 💖 Sorry Website: A Diwali Special

An interactive, romantic web experience built with React. It walks through a story of memories with photos and messages, asks a heartfelt question, and ends with a Diwali blessing and a glowing anar (firecracker) night scene.

## 🔗 Live Demo

**👉 [https://sorry31.netlify.app](https://sorry31.netlify.app)**

Best experienced on a phone or laptop with sound on 🔊

---

## ✨ Features

- 📸 **Memory story:** photos with heartfelt messages, with **Previous** and **Next** buttons to move through them
- 🎶 **Background music:** starts on the first tap, with a button in the bottom-right corner to mute or unmute
- 💌 **Question screen:** an interactive Yes / No question
- 🎉 **Celebration screen:** a happy ending that leads into the Diwali surprise
- 🪔 **Diwali blessing:** a decorated card where each wish appears one by one, with twinkling lights and floating sparkles
- 🎆 **Blow the Firecracker:** a night scene with a glowing anar pot, a burning fuse, a sparks fountain and fireworks, including heart-shaped bursts. Tap anywhere to launch your own
- 💗 Floating hearts, teddies and candies in the background

---

## 🛠️ Tech Stack

| Technology | Use |
| --- | --- |
| [React](https://react.dev/) | UI and screen flow |
| [Vite](https://vitejs.dev/) | Fast dev server and build tool |
| [Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/) | Styling |
| HTML Canvas | Sparks and fireworks animation |
| [Netlify](https://www.netlify.com/) | Hosting |

---

## 📁 Project Structure

```
p/
├── public/
│   └── music.mp3            # background music
├── src/
│   ├── assets/images/       # photos used in the story
│   ├── components/
│   │   ├── Navbar.jsx
│   │   ├── FloatingElements.jsx
│   │   ├── Frame.jsx        # photo + message card (Previous / Next)
│   │   ├── Question.jsx
│   │   ├── FinalScreen.jsx
│   │   ├── DiwaliScreen.jsx # Diwali blessing
│   │   ├── AnarScreen.jsx   # anar and fireworks scene
│   │   └── MusicPlayer.jsx
│   ├── data/story.js        # images and messages for each frame
│   ├── App.jsx              # controls the flow between screens
│   └── main.jsx
└── package.json
```

---

## 🚀 Run Locally

The app lives inside the `p` folder.

```bash
# 1. Clone the repository
git clone <your-repo-url>

# 2. Go into the app folder
cd <repo-folder>/p

# 3. Install dependencies
npm install

# 4. Start the dev server
npm run dev
```

Then open **http://localhost:5173** in your browser.

### Build for production

```bash
npm run build
```

The output goes to the `dist` folder.

---

## 🌐 Deployment

Deployed on **Netlify** from this GitHub repository.

| Setting | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Base directory | `p` |
| Build command | `npm run build` |
| Publish directory | `dist` |

Every push to the main branch redeploys the site automatically.

---

## ✏️ Customize

- **Photos and messages:** edit `src/data/story.js` and put your images in `src/assets/images/`
- **Music:** replace `public/music.mp3`
- **Diwali wish:** edit the `lines` list in `src/components/DiwaliScreen.jsx`
- **Timing:** change `GAP` in `DiwaliScreen.jsx` (pause between sentences) and `IGNITE` in `AnarScreen.jsx` (when the anar lights)

---

## 📝 Note

The audio autoplay policy of browsers means music starts only after the first tap or click on the page.

